	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Claude Code Launcher

Launch VS Code or Claude Code in your project directories.

### Keywords
- `vs` - Open project in VS Code
- `cc` - Open project in Claude Code (Terminal)
- `gh` - Open project on GitHub
- `review &lt;pr-url&gt; [prompt]` - Start Claude Code in a `.claude/worktrees/pr-&lt;n&gt;` worktree holding the PR head and run the `/review-pr` skill (any optional prompt is appended as extra instruction)
- `implement-issue &lt;issue-url&gt; [prompt]` - Start Claude Code in a fresh `.claude/worktrees/issue-&lt;n&gt;` worktree and run the `/implement-issue` skill: implement, push a draft PR, self-review (any optional prompt is appended as extra instruction)

`review` and `implement-issue` need the `review-pr` and `implement-issue` skills installed in `~/.claude/skills` (`task install-skills` in the repo).

### Configuration
Set the `project_dirs` workflow variable to a colon-separated list of directories:

Example: `~/src/github.com/fredsmith:~/claude-working`

Set `launch_mode` to `window` (open a terminal) or `background` (`claude --bg`, then manage sessions with `claude agents`).

### Modifiers
- `Cmd+Enter` - Reveal project in Finder</string>
